import AFTD.Prelude

/-!
# slow_mode_dephasing

Topic: statistical_mechanics   Node: 8c669bb38ad5

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2609.13387, Eq. (89)

For permutations in the symmetric group S_n, with H the average of left-regular permutation matrices for all m-cycles, kappa_{n,m}(s) is the sum over g in S_n of |(exp(-i * s * H))_{g, 1}|^2 * (fix(g) - 1) / (n - 1), where fix(g) is the number of fixed points of g in {0, ..., n-1}.
-/

/-- Standard-irrep dephasing factor kappa_{n,m}(s) = sum_{g in S_n} |(exp(-i s H))_{g,1}|^2 (fix(g) - 1)/(n - 1) for the continuous-time quantum walk on S_n generated by m-cycles. -/
noncomputable def slow_mode_dephasing (n m : ℕ) (s : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  let H : Matrix (Equiv.Perm (Fin n)) (Equiv.Perm (Fin n)) ℂ :=
    fun g h ↦ if (g * h⁻¹).cycleType = {m} then
      ((({c : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) | c.cycleType = {m}} : Finset (Equiv.Perm (Fin n))).card : ℂ)⁻¹)
    else 0
  ∑ g : Equiv.Perm (Fin n),
    ‖(NormedSpace.exp (- (Complex.I * (s : ℂ)) • H)) g 1‖ ^ 2 *
      ((((Finset.filter (fun i : Fin n ↦ g i = i) Finset.univ).card : ℝ) - 1) / ((n : ℝ) - 1))
